well, I can tell you that my game got significantly easier once I was
able to mow down monsters with Mojo.  When soldier ants die in two
hits rather than six, it totally changes how you can play the game.
Instead of writing Elbereth everywhere, it's easier to just kill the
stupid monster.    I wound up blowing up a few wands being carried by
my enemies, but that's easily a positive tradeoff.  I lost maybe two
wands of magic missile and one wand of create monster in favor of
being able to walk up to any monster and give it a critical jolt with
Thor's hammer.  and then the tourist quest gives you more loot than
you know what to do with, so a few missing wands doesn't even get
noticed.

Before you get strength bonuses and scrolls of enchant weapon,
Mjollnir is probably the most damaging weapon out there.  I really
like Grayswandir, but at +0 and strength 14, can anything beat Mojo?

I almost never throw Mjollnir.  As a valk I might if there's a mind
flayer a few squares away and I don't care much about my rings, but
you have to come up with a narrow set of parameters where throwing
Mojo is better than all of your other options (like burning Elbereth
with a wand of fire and then using wands/missiles/daggers).

Anyway, I am utterly convinced that Mjollnir is one of the better
weapons for a young tourist.  Pray that you receive that and not
Giantslayer.


